{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Measurement findings: is `derive_caused_by` reliable for this codebase's history?\n\nAll numbers below were produced in worktree `work-50e3` (HEAD at current `origin/main`) with the\nworktree `.venv` interpreter, read-only against the live tracker and full git history.\n\n### Method (reproducible)\n\n**Step 1 — population.** Reduce every ticket directory under\n`rebar.config.tracker_dir(repo_root)` with `rebar.reducer.reduce_ticket`; select\n`ticket_type == \"bug\"`, `status == \"closed\"`, with ≥1 active `caused_by` dep. Result:\n**782 bugs total, 760 closed, 88 closed bugs carrying a `caused_by` edge** — the whole\npopulation, no sampling.\n\n**Step 2 — re-run the real deriver on each.** For each of the 88, call the actual mechanism and\nannotate abstentions with the observable failure reason:\n\n```python\nimport os, json\nfrom rebar import config\nfrom rebar.metrics.blame import derive_caused_by, _find_fixing_commit\nfrom rebar._engine_support import field_reads\nrepo_root = os.getcwd(); tracker = str(config.tracker_dir(repo_root))\nfor r in population:               # the 88 closed bugs with caused_by edges\n    derived = derive_caused_by(r[\"id\"], repo_root, tracker)\n    if derived is None:\n        fixing = _find_fixing_commit(repo_root, r[\"id\"], tracker)\n        if not fixing: reason = \"no-fixing-commit\"\n        elif not [p for e in field_reads.file_impact(r[\"id\"], tracker)\n                  if (p := (e or {}).get(\"path\"))]: reason = \"no-file-impact\"\n        else: reason = \"no-majority-or-unresolvable\"\n    # classify: derived in r[\"targets\"] → agree; else disagree; None → abstain\n```\n\n### Result — population bound (n = 88)\n\n| classification | n | share | abstain-reason breakdown |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| agree (derived ∈ recorded) | 38 | 43% | — |\n| disagree (derived ∉ recorded) | 6 | 7% | — |\n| abstain (derived = None) | 44 | 50% | no-majority-or-unresolvable 33, no-file-impact 8, no-fixing-commit 3 |\n\nAs the plan requires, this table is a **bound, not a supplied-vs-derived identification**: the\nrecorded edge carries no provenance marker (`_apply_caused_by` writes via `_write_link_event`\nwith no derived-vs-explicit field — src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py), so \"agree\" means\nonly *consistent with* blame-derivation, and disagree/abstain means *not reproducible by the\nderiver today* (history drift is a live confounder: 3 fixing commits no longer resolve, 8\ntickets carry an edge but no file_impact path the deriver can blame, and reformat/move carriers\nlanded since close can dissolve a majority that existed at close time).\n\nNotable structure in the 6 disagreements: **5 of the 6 share the same recorded target**\n(`ed5c-42fc-bb7f-4cf4`, \"No guard makes an unsigned, identity-less writer loud\") with five\n*different* derived targets — a batch attribution of a guard-gap bug family to one origin\nticket, exactly the many-bugs-one-cause shape where per-bug file blame scatters. None of those\nfive tickets' prose independently proves the ed5c attribution, so they are excluded from the\naccuracy subsample below, but the cluster is direct evidence that when a *family* of bugs is\nattributed to one origin, the deriver would have scattered the attribution across unrelated\ntickets had the edges not been supplied.\n\n### Result — accuracy against proven origins (subsample n = 8)\n\nGround truth: the ten attributions this ticket's original description table established under\n`/rebar-debug` (each with a proven mechanism), plus `aragonite-bleached-vipersquid` (17c3),\nwhose root-cause comment names `789c-1251-fc21-4cf6`. Two of the ten are outside the\npopulation (`steep-tired-whimbrel` carries no caused_by edge today;\n`nonodorous-snotty-seaurchin` was proven unattributable, so correctly has no edge). For the\nremaining **8**, every recorded edge matches the proven origin (they were supplied per the\ndebug protocol). The deriver's score against that ground truth:\n\n| bug | proven origin | deriver today | verdict | defect shape |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| bediasite-bilineate-stoat | cec6-0a0e | None (no-majority-or-unresolvable) | abstained | omission at origin (single commit — blame *was* predicted correct; drift since) |\n| perkish-balsamic-pupfish | fc20-2df1 | None (no-majority-or-unresolvable) | abstained | unmet obligation (fc20 never touched gates.py) |\n| irongrey-chubby-oxpecker | 789c-1251 | None (no-file-impact) | abstained | unmet obligation (consumer vs producer contract) |\n| moist-short-lionfish | c1de-d6a0 | **e1f4-d518** | **wrong-target** | unmet obligation — named exactly the innocent producer the original table predicted blame would name |\n| electronic-deducible-maggot | 8d36-a15a | None (no-file-impact) | abstained | carrier commit (June file-move) |\n| itchy-arbored-peccary | b73c + 615c | None (no-majority-or-unresolvable) | abstained | omission (ADR promise no AC obliged) |\n| ruling-magnific-bats | 555e-3efa | None (no-majority-or-unresolvable) | abstained | cause site IS fix site (blame predicted correct; drift since) |\n| aragonite-bleached-vipersquid | 789c-1251 | None (no-majority-or-unresolvable) | abstained | unmet obligation (789c moved decode composition one side only) |\n\n**Correct 0 / wrong-target 1 / abstained 7.** On the only bugs where ground truth is\nindependently proven, the deriver reproduced **none** of the correct attributions, and the one\ntime it spoke confidently it named the innocent party — the producer whose code was correct\nwhen written (`e1f4` wrote `pending_enrichment` for drain-time enumeration; `c1de` put it on\nthe write path under a self-declared 20 ms budget). The proportion of blame-derivable edges in\nthis subsample naming a defensibly wrong origin is therefore **1/1 of its confident outputs**\n(and 1/8 of the subsample; the other 7 fail closed).\n\n### Decision (a): should a blame-derived edge be distinguishable on read from a supplied one? — YES\n\nThis measurement is itself the strongest evidence: with 88 edges and no provenance field, the\ncentral question \"how many of these are guesses?\" is **unanswerable** — the study could only\nbound it (38 consistent-with-blame vs 50 not-reproducible-today). Every consumer of the edge\n(escape-rate lenses, the epic-close `caused_by` floor, any future reviewer) inherits that\nambiguity. A `derived: blame | explicit` marker on the link event would cost one field at\nwrite time and make the metric's confidence computable. Filed as a proposal ticket\n(discovered_from this one) for operator adjudication — not implemented here.\n\n### Decision (b): should the fallback decline to attribute for shapes it cannot get right? — Keep fail-closed as-is; do NOT add shape detection; discount rather than delete\n\nReasoning from the numbers:\n- The fallback **already declines** in the hard cases: 50% abstention on the population, 7/8 on\n  the proven subsample. The strict >50% majority rule is doing exactly the fail-closed work the\n  design intended, and the dominant shapes here (unmet obligation, carrier, omission) mostly\n  land in abstention, not misattribution.\n- The residual risk is the confident-but-wrong case (moist-short-lionfish; plus the ed5c\n  cluster's scattered would-be targets): when the shape is \"consumer edited last, producer\n  innocent\", file-majority blame returns a confident wrong answer *by construction*, and no\n  mechanical signal inside blame distinguishes it — the deriver cannot know the defect shape\n  without understanding the mechanism, which is precisely what the human/debug protocol\n  supplies. So \"decline for shapes it cannot get right\" is not implementable as stated: shape\n  is not observable to the mechanism.\n- The implementable version is decision (a): mark derived edges, and let consumers weight or\n  exclude them (e.g. metrics report supplied-vs-derived escape rates separately). That\n  preserves the 38 agreements (harmless where blame is right, e.g. single-commit omissions)\n  while quarantining the guesses. A behaviour change to the deriver itself is NOT recommended\n  on this evidence.\n\n### Limitations (named, per plan)\n\n- **History drift:** the deriver ran today, not at close time. Abstentions include cases blame\n  may have answered (possibly correctly) at close — bediasite and ruling-magnific-bats were\n  predicted blame-correct and now abstain. The 0/8 correct figure is therefore a *today* figure;\n  it understates close-time accuracy by an unknown amount, but the wrong-target case is\n  drift-independent (e1f4 was the wrong answer then and now).\n- **Agreement is a bound:** with no provenance marker, the 38 agreements cannot be split into\n  \"blame agreed with a proof\" vs \"blame agreeing with itself\".\n- **Subsample bias:** the 8 proven origins all come from one session's `/rebar-debug` work and\n  over-represent the hard shapes (that session is why the question was asked). They are the\n  only ground truth available, not a random sample.\n- The verdict is correspondingly scoped: **the fallback's fail-closed behaviour is working; its\n  confident answers are unverifiable in bulk and were wrong when verifiable; the missing piece\n  is provenance, not a smarter guesser.**"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787395114255832001,"uuid":"20ea455f-fe98-4c5b-a573-2a082a8684a3"}